    {
      "dom_id": "question-81891",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(X∧Y)⇒Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(X∧Y)⇒Y≡¬(¬(X∧Y))∨Y.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(X∧Y))∨Y≡(X∧Y)∨Y.\n$$\n\nFinally, by the absorption law, we have\n\n$$\n(X∧Y)∨Y≡Y.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $Y.$",
